    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output tonight, led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, whose elite 80.98 score makes him our premier start. Facing Lowder (4.77 xERA), **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a perfect storm of favorable park factors, a strong platoon advantage, and\u2014crucially for our scarcity-driven strategy\u2014a 100% stolen base expectation against a slow pitcher delivery. **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (68.40) and **Lars Nootbaar** (64.54) follow as secondary anchors; **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** enjoys an ideal combination of park and platoon boosts against Lopez, while **Lars Nootbaar** gains significant value from an assumed leadoff role and favorable wind conditions that inflate his scoring potential beyond his base projection.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Carson Benge** (59.08), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Carson Benge** offers a strong profile, he was edged out by the superior efficiency and stolen base upside of **Kyle Schwarber** and **Christian Yelich**. We are also closely monitoring the lineup status of **Trea Turner**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**; should any of these core contributors be dropped from their assumed spots, their efficiency scores\u2014and our overall category floor\u2014will need immediate reassessment. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the SP matchups. **Dillon Dingler** faces the toughest test of the day against Skubal (2.74 xERA), and his score of 48.50 reflects that volatility; he remains a marginal start, held primarily for his order placement. Meanwhile, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Caleb Durbin**, and **Chase Meidroth** hover in the 42\u201348 range. While these players are active, they are currently functioning at the lower bound of our Roto efficiency requirements. We are bypassing **Colt Keith**, **Gary Sanchez**, and **Casey Schmitt** entirely today due to injury or lack of confirmed lineup availability, ensuring our game caps are strictly preserved for the most favorable statistical matchups.",
